.TH CRAFTHUB 1 "" "Craft Hub" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crafthub \- install, update and uninstall the Crafting Apps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crafthub
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Craft Hub is a manager for the ArtCraft Crafting Apps (PhotoCraft, VectorCraft, DesignCraft,
LightCraft, FilmCraft, EffectCraft, PDFCraft and ArtCraft). Without options it opens its window.
Apps are installed for the current user only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-install " ID"
Install an app, for example \fIphotocraft\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-update " ID|all"
Update an app, or every installed app.
.TP
.BI \-\-uninstall " ID"
Uninstall an app.
.TP
.BI \-\-delete\-data " ID"
Delete an uninstalled app's settings and saved data.
.TP
.BI \-\-open " ID"
Open an installed app.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Show installed apps.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Show the latest release of each app.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show Craft Hub's version.
.TP
.BR \-\-uninstall\-self " [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-purge ]
Uninstall Craft Hub (with \fB\-\-all\fR, also every app it installed; with \fB\-\-purge\fR,
also their settings and saved data). The packaged Craft Hub is removed with
\fBapt-get purge crafthub\fR, which asks for your password.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/crafthub
Installed apps and Craft Hub's own data.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/crafthub.sources
Craft Hub's software source, through which updates arrive. Removing the package keeps it, so
Craft Hub stays available in Software Manager; purging removes it.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/keyrings/crafthub.gpg
The key Craft Hub's software source is signed with.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/TymonDomanko/CraftHub
